# 03 Results: high-frequency buzz (80–249 Hz motor current, big three joints)

Generated by `analysis.py`. 40663 windows of 0.25 s from 134 real-arm bags (V5–V9b). Units: /joint_states effort as published by the UR driver (motor current, A).

## Buzz by output mode (moving windows)

| Mode | windows | median (A) | p95 (A) | max (A) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| position | 6460 | 0.098 | 0.883 | 4.169 |
| trajectory | 5577 | 0.091 | 0.254 | 0.959 |
| velocity | 11017 | 0.138 | 1.640 | 5.490 |
| velocity_optimised | 4924 | 0.110 | 1.728 | 6.041 |
| velocity_unfiltered | 714 | 0.374 | 0.849 | 1.110 |

Floor (still windows, all modes): median 0.060 A, p95 0.102 A.

## Same input (V7 LargeVibrations recording, replayed on 11-06)

| Run | mode | median (A) | p95 (A) | max (A) |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| V7/LargeVibrations (original, velocity) | velocity_optimised | 1.733 | 5.362 | 6.041 |
| V9b position replay | position | 0.556 | 1.198 | 1.369 |
| V9b trajectory replay | trajectory | 0.106 | 0.147 | 0.199 |

## Pose dependence (velocity and position output, moving windows)

Joints that best separate the top-5 % buzz windows from the rest (standardised mean difference): shoulder_lift_joint 0.59, shoulder_pan_joint 0.20, wrist_3_joint 0.20, elbow_joint 0.19.
Rank correlation of buzz with the 80–249 Hz content of the joint-velocity command: 0.38 (n = 23041 windows). Low = the arm/drive produces the buzz without it being in the command.

Limit: /joint_states at 500 Hz cannot see above 250 Hz; anything higher aliases into this band.

## Prior claims checked

- "speedj-only and pose-dependent"; "V9b position 0.32–0.35 A vs trajectory 0.055 A in 80–249 Hz": see the tables (different window definition: 0.25 s windows, big three joints, moving only).

